-- title:
--   The Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion for R ≅ T
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal; let $R$ be a commutative local Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal; and let $T$ be a commutative local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Let $\varphi : R \to T$ be a surjective homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, and let $\pi_R : R \to \mathcal{O}$ and $\pi_T : T \to \mathcal{O}$ be $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphisms with $\pi_T \circ \varphi = \pi_R$. Write $\eta_T = \pi_T\bigl(\operatorname{Ann}_T(\ker \pi_T)\bigr)$ for the ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ generated by the image under $\pi_T$ of the annihilator of the ideal $\ker \pi_T$, and let $(\ker \pi_R)/(\ker \pi_R)^2$ be the cotangent module of $\ker \pi_R$. Assume $\eta_T \neq 0$ and that the $\mathcal{O}$-module length of $(\ker \pi_R)/(\ker \pi_R)^2$ is at most the $\mathcal{O}$-module length of $\mathcal{O}/\eta_T$ (lengths taken in $\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$). Then $\varphi$ is bijective, and there are a natural number $n$ and elements $f_0,\dots,f_{n-1}$ of the $n$-variable formal power series ring $\mathcal{O}[[X_0,\dots,X_{n-1}]]$ such that $T$ is isomorphic, as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, to the quotient of that power series ring by the ideal generated by the $f_i$.
--
--   This is the numerical criterion of Wiles, in the form given by Lenstra and by de Smit–Rubin–Schoof: a surjection $R \to T$ of augmented $\mathcal{O}$-algebras whose cotangent module at the augmentation is no longer than $\mathcal{O}/\eta_T$ is an isomorphism, and $T$ is then a complete intersection, presented by $n$ relations in $n$ power series variables. It is pure commutative algebra, applied in the Taylor–Wiles argument with $R$ a deformation ring and $T$ a Hecke algebra, and is used here in the construction of the patching data attached to a Frey curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgHom_bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le.lean

